Copyright 2026 Summon Software Labs.

This product includes software developed by Summon Software Labs.

The Cooling Failure Manager source tree contains no third-party source code. It
builds and tests with a C++20 compiler and CMake alone, with no network access
and no downloaded dependencies. The only non-standard-library interfaces it uses
are operating-system facilities for file creation, file replacement, file
sizing, file flushing and whole-file locking; those are provided by the host
operating system and are not distributed with this repository.

The library performs no I/O of its own except when a caller opens a durable
store, and it never performs cooling actuation of any kind. It classifies
cooling failure, decides which protective response is justified and evaluates
recovery gates from evidence the caller supplies; every response it reports is a
bounded request addressed to the component that owns the equipment.

Cooling Failure Manager does not collect or transmit any telemetry. Every record
it writes is written to local files chosen by the operator and never leaves the
machine running the software.

